# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL DEV against the SHARED DEV Convex deployment (no Coolify wait)
#
# Copy this to .env.local and fill in the <<< PASTE >>> values. Next.js loads
# .env.local OVER .env, so these override your normal .env. This is the same
# "lie about the domain" auth bridge the PR previews use, run locally: your local
# app mints Better Auth tokens that the shared dev Convex deployment validates,
# because they share the signing keypair (same DB) + issuer (BETTER_AUTH_URL).
#
# Why it works without a tunnel: the shared dev Convex deployment fetches JWKS
# from https://preview.lab.rvlt.app/api/auth/jwks (the always-on preview app) —
# it never calls your local machine. Your local app just needs to sign with the
# same keypair (same DB + secret) and stamp the same issuer.
#
# Trade-off: uses the SHARED DEV Postgres, so local dev reads/writes the same
# data as the PR previews. OAuth + passkeys don't work here — use email/password.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Same DB as the previews → same Better Auth signing keypair (jwks table).
# Value = GitHub secret / Coolify env PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL (shared dev Postgres).
DATABASE_URL="<<< PASTE PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL >>>"

# Same secret → can sign/decrypt with that shared keypair.
# Value = GitHub secret PREVIEW_BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (matches the always-on
# preview.lab.rvlt.app app).
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="<<< PASTE PREVIEW_BETTER_AUTH_SECRET >>>"

# The "lie": the issuer the shared dev Convex deployment trusts
# (its CONVEX_AUTH_ISSUER = https://preview.lab.rvlt.app). Do not change.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="https://preview.lab.rvlt.app"

# Keep the browser + CSRF on your real host. This value is in trustedOrigins
# (src/lib/auth.ts) and the session cookie scopes to the request host, not the
# lie. Use whatever host you open the dev server at (localhost, roger, LAN IP…).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://roger:3000"

# Talk to the shared dev Convex deployment. Find the real URL in the Convex
# dashboard → dev deployment (the value below is only an example).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL="https://groovy-koala-475.convex.cloud"
